menu "LittleFS on UBI Example Configuration"

    config EXAMPLE_FORMAT_IF_MOUNT_FAILED
        bool "Format the flash if mount failed"
        default y
        help
            If this config item is set, format_if_mount_failed will be set to true and
            the LittleFS volume will be formatted if the first mount attempt fails (e.g.
            on a factory-blank chip with no prior LittleFS superblock).

    config EXAMPLE_WIPE_NAND_ON_BOOT
        bool "Erase the whole NAND chip on boot (destroys all data)"
        default n
        help
            Erases every good block of the raw NAND before attaching UBI, so the
            attach sees a blank chip and nand_ubi_get_blockdev() creates one volume
            spanning the whole chip. Use for one boot to measure the full-chip case,
            then disable it again: with it enabled, every boot starts from scratch.
endmenu
